@vsm 1.0
// EXP-G-01/spec.vsm — Ω-slack census: measure g (the only unmeasured V ingredient) incl. ethics
// domain_context: {target=vsf-nucleus, env=analysis, layer=L+2}
// date: 2026-06-15 | status: PRE-REGISTERED (hypotheses fixed before running)
// suite: certifier-validation (with EXP-VNC-01, EXP-CORE-01) | binary: omega_slack_census (main.rs, TBD)

spec(EXP-G-01, "per-constraint Ω-slack census — measuring g, and 'ethics as geometry'"):

  motivation:
    "g = mínᵢ(normalised slack of Aᵢ) is the ONLY ingredient of V = min(g,c,t,m) that the paper
     ASSERTS (g≈1) rather than measures (c=EXP-LY-01, t=EXP-TDA-01, m=EXP-NS-01, p=stasis_cos).
     Worse, the paper's strong claim — violating A0 ⇒ g→0 ⇒ V=0 (ethics as a face of Ω) — is never
     demonstrated. EXP-G-01 extracts the per-constraint slacks from omega_validator.rs and shows
     g binds when a constraint (including the ethical faces) is approached or violated."

  model:
    "For each principal constraint Aᵢ of Ω (paper §3): A0 (purpose∩prohibited=∅), A0.1 (coercion=0),
     A3 (B(task)≤B_available, budget/Ashby), A5 (autonomy≤ceiling(S5), governance), Aε (H_KS≤H_max,
     entropy). Define the normalised slack:
        slackᵢ = (boundary value − current value) / (constraint scale)  ∈ (−∞, 1]
     slack=1 fully satisfied, slack=0 at the boundary, slack<0 violated.
     g = mínᵢ slackᵢ ; clamp to [0,1] for the V signature (g<0 ⇒ g=0 ⇒ V=0)."

  procedure:
    phase_1_baseline:
      "At the warmed-up attractor, read every constraint slack from omega_validator telemetry.
       Report the slack vector and g = min slack. Expect all slacks > 0, g large (≈1) — the kernel
       sits comfortably inside Ω."
    phase_2_constraint_approach:
      "Drive ONE constraint at a time toward its boundary and record slackᵢ → g → V:
         A3: raise B(task) past B_available.
         A5: push autonomy past the S5 ceiling.
         Aε: drive H_KS past H_max.
       Expect slackᵢ→0→<0, g→0, and V=min(g,c,t,m)→0 even while c,t,m stay ≈1."
    phase_3_ethics_demonstration:
      "The key phase. Inject a synthetic state with purpose∩prohibited≠∅ (A0) or coercion>0 (A0.1)
       — the kernel will not violate ethics spontaneously. Show the ethical face IS expressible as
       a numeric slack and that violating it sends g→0 ⇒ V=0. This turns 'ethics as geometry' from
       an assertion into a measurement."

  hypotheses (pre-registered):
    H_G1: "at the attractor all slacks > 0 and g = min slack ≈ 1 (comfortably feasible)."
    H_G2: "driving any single constraint to its boundary sends g→0 monotonically (g tracks the
           binding constraint, as a min must)."
    H_G3 (ethics): "a state violating A0 or A0.1 yields slack<0 on that face ⇒ g=0 ⇒ V=0,
           regardless of c,t,m. The operational content of 'ethics is a face of Ω', measured."
    H_G4 (g ≠ p): "a state can have high cos to the attractor (p≈1) yet g<0 (constraint/ethics
           violated) — confirming g is NOT redundant with p (the rev.1 V error that g was added to fix)."

  deliverable:
    "The per-constraint slack vector at the attractor (g MEASURED, closing the V-signature hole) +
     a g-vs-constraint-approach curve showing g binds and V collapses + the ethics demonstration
     (A0 violation ⇒ V=0). Makes the g row of the §capstone signature table a measurement and
     'ethics as geometry' a measured fact."

  paper_impact:
    "§capstone (g row measured, not asserted) + §certifier / the A0-fail-closed discussion
     (ethics-as-Ω-face demonstrated) + §What-VSF-models (the Q1 feasible-region step instantiated)."

  implementation_notes:
    "omega_validator.rs computes Ω membership; per-constraint MARGINS may need exposing as telemetry
     (omega.margin.A0, .A3, .A5, .Aε …) — pre-register this as the first implementation step. The A0/A0.1
     ethics slacks require a synthetic-state injection path (the kernel won't self-violate). Analysis-only."

⟦ /EXP-G-01-spec | vsm-1.0 | 2026-06-15 | PRE-REGISTERED ⟧
